from pathlib import Path
import json,shutil,hashlib,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
RUN=ROOT/'ada_run/encounter_pilot/Random_Entropy/entropy-columns'
for p in RUN.glob('*.png'):shutil.copy2(p,HERE/p.name)
shutil.copy2(RUN/'report.json',HERE/'museum-report.json')
reports=[json.loads((HERE/n).read_text(encoding='utf8')) for n in ['verification.json','museum-report.json']]
assert all(r['passed'] and not r['failures'] for r in reports)
counts=[len(r['checks']) for r in reports]
style='''*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#e7ecec;color:#24363e;font:18px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1420px;margin:auto;padding:30px}h1{font:clamp(36px,5vw,62px)/1.1 Georgia,serif}h2{font:30px/1.2 Georgia,serif}p{max-width:85ch}a{color:#285e70}nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px}figure{margin:0}img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figcaption{padding:14px;background:#d8e0e1;font-size:16px}section{margin:36px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:22px}.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}@media(max-width:850px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.four{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}'''
def figure(name,caption):return f'<figure><img src="{html.escape(name)}.png" width="1600" height="1050" alt="{html.escape(caption)}" loading="lazy"><figcaption>{html.escape(caption)}</figcaption></figure>'
body='''<h1>Four states at body scale</h1><p>Two-metre glass columns replace the tabletop jars. Matching proportions, muted red and blue beads, matte bases and thin metal collars keep attention on the arrangements. The room wall supplies a quieter background; readings sit on a separate side panel.</p>'''+figure('columns-front','Native front comparison with an orthographic camera. Equal projected scale; this is a supplied comparison view, not a headset view.')+'''<section><h2>The same record, a larger view</h2><p>Every column retains the original seed-435 coordinates: forty red and forty blue beads. Only the display mapping changes. Bead centres expand horizontally and vertically, while the beads themselves stay round. Both entropy readings match the earlier jar records exactly.</p><div class="grid four">'''+''.join(figure('column-'+str(i+1),c) for i,c in enumerate(['A / Layers','B / Interface','C / Mixed','D / Core and shell']))+'''</div></section><section class="grid">'''+figure('columns-in-room','Perspective view in the installed Entropy Workshop. The table and broad backdrop are gone; front and rear inspection positions are clear.')+figure('reading-panel','A small wall-supported side panel keeps the measurements separate from the specimens.')+'''</section><section><h2>From the previous jars</h2>'''+figure('../2026-10-16-entropy-reading/four-jars','Earlier tabletop version, retained as the comparison baseline.')+f'''<p>{counts[0]} apparatus checks verify unchanged coordinates, unchanged readings, round non-emissive beads and containment. {counts[1]} installed-room checks verify floor support and clear front/rear approaches, including the side panel. The map pathfinder passes. Headset readability and the effect on a visitor’s interpretation still need a human trial.</p></section><nav><a href="verification.json">Apparatus checks</a><a href="museum-report.json">Room checks</a><a href="manifest.json">Source fingerprints</a><a href="../2026-10-16-entropy-reading/index.html">Two-hall plan</a><a href="/long-museum/writing-wall?map=Random_Entropy">Writing wall</a></nav><p>Restart the museum to load the columns in Entropy Workshop (Random_Entropy), at the existing comparison placement (3,2). The original hand-sized shakeable jar remains nearby.</p>'''
(HERE/'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Four column states · Ada Research</title><style>'+style+'</style><main>'+body+'</main></html>',encoding='utf8')
files=[ROOT/'commons/artifacts/ordinary_entropies'/n for n in ['jar_states.gd','jar_column.gd','jar_snapshot.gd']]+[ROOT/'commons/maps/Random_Entropy'/n for n in ['map_data.json','writing_wall.json','tutorial.md','final.md','plan.md']]
(HERE/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks':counts,'display':{'height_m':2.0,'radius_m':0.34,'bead_radius_m':0.032},'retained_record':{'height_m':0.34,'radius_m':0.13,'seed':435,'counts':[40,40]},'sha256':{p.relative_to(ROOT).as_posix():hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in files}},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(HERE/'README.md').write_text('''# Full-size entropy columns

Palle asks for full-size columns and a restrained scientific appearance. The original four small-jar records remain unchanged. A display adapter maps them into two-metre columns with round beads, fixed colours, faint height divisions, matte plinths and metal collars. A separate side panel replaces the broad backing. The placement rotates to face the quieter entrance wall; front/rear approaches remain reachable. Source bodies are hidden with collision disabled; the full-size columns provide physical boundaries.

The first native render looked into the busy workshop and the front overview stood too close to its entrance wall. Rotating the bank made the main background quieter and supplied clear standing space. Final native images were inspected; no generated mock-ups are used. The orthographic image is an explicitly labelled comparison camera, not visitor evidence.

Run `python -X utf8 doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-entropy-columns/run.py`; then `python -X utf8 tools/run_encounter_probe.py Random_Entropy --sequence randomness --render --no-bridges --output-tag entropy-columns --probe doc/book/iterations/2026-10-16-entropy-columns/museum_probe.gd`; then the map pathfinder and publish.py. Current checks: '''+str(counts)+''', both Godot processes exit 0. Headset comfort and human reading remain open. The original live jar, prefab controls, saves, gallery, replay, hall relationship and first 48-value pilot are unchanged.
''',encoding='utf8')
print('Published column review:',counts)
